// Travel destinations (v0.979): named world places for quest Travel
// objectives. A Travel step is done while the player stands within `radius`
// metres of the place AND it is the step they are on (2026-10-04,
// systems::quests::destinations_here): walking past a place before the step
// that asks for it does not count, and standing in it when the step comes up
// does. A fixed place's `pos` is across the floor only (x and z,
// homestead-world frame - the same frame entities/wild_spawns.ron uses): it
// has no height, and counts from any height over it. The places in `at`
// below have a FLOOR, and `radius` is measured across the floor only while
// the player stands on that floor's storey (ship homes increment 7, 2026-10-20:
// feet from half a metre under the floor to half a metre under the place's
// top, src/ship/moves.rs `stands_in_storey_of`): a place on an upper floor is
// never reached by standing under it.
//
// A place that is not a fixed point names what it resolves to in `at`
// instead of a `pos` (2026-10-04, the opening's last step):
//   OwnFrontDoor(out_m: m)   the doorstep `m` metres out of the player's OWN
//                            front door, along the corridor its plot's door
//                            makes: on the Commons for a family home's plot,
//                            on the street for a First Street plot, whichever
//                            plot the player was given; on the corridor's
//                            floor. A guest (no plot, the home put away) has
//                            none, so it never resolves.
//   NearestVolume(zone_type: t)
//                            the floor of the ship's labelled volume of zone
//                            type t (data/blueprints/zone_types.ron; a row of a
//                            zone body's `zones` in the ship file, like the
//                            Commons' "mess-hall") NEAREST the player's own front
//                            door, so each home is sent to the one that serves
//                            it; for a guest, the one nearest where they stand.
//                            Nearest on the storey it is measured from (the
//                            door's floor, the guest's feet): the nearest of
//                            the volumes on that storey, and only when none is
//                            on it the nearest on any.
//                            Never a room of the player's own home. `radius` is
//                            then how far past the edge of that floor still
//                            counts: anywhere on it does (2026-10-12, ship homes
//                            increment 6, the Cabin's opening).
//
// Adding a landmark = adding a row here; reference it from any quest file
// as Travel(destination: "<id>").
(
    destinations: [
        // Just outside the player's own front door (the opening, data/quests/
        // getting_started.ron). 1.5 m out with a 1.5 m radius: it spans the
        // 3 m door corridor from the doorway outward, and the spawn just
        // inside the door (data/homes/homestead.ron, 1.5 m in) is 3 m from
        // its centre, so waking up there is not "stepping out".
        (id: "front_door", label: "your front door", at: Some(OwnFrontDoor(out_m: 1.5)), radius: 1.5),
        // The mess hall that serves the player's home, and the recreation room
        // (the Cabin's opening, data/quests/getting_started.ron): the Commons'
        // for the cabin row, the South Commons' for a homestead far down First
        // Street. On the floor or within a metre of its edge: the mess hall is
        // a 30 m strip whose stores stand at one end, so no circle round its
        // middle would do.
        (id: "mess_hall", label: "the mess hall", at: Some(NearestVolume(zone_type: "mess_hall")), radius: 1.0),
        (id: "recreation", label: "the recreation room", at: Some(NearestVolume(zone_type: "recreation")), radius: 1.0),
        // The outdoor crop fields just south of the house.
        (id: "outdoor_fields", label: "the outdoor fields", pos: (29.0, 63.0), radius: 10.0),
        // The berry thicket northeast of the fields (wild_spawns berry_bush cluster).
        (id: "wild_thicket", label: "the berry thicket", pos: (52.0, 82.0), radius: 8.0),
        // The flax stand near the wetter ground west of the thicket.
        (id: "flax_hollow", label: "the flax hollow", pos: (18.0, 88.0), radius: 8.0),
        // The ridge northeast where the wolves den (hostile wildlife setting).
        (id: "wolf_ridge", label: "the northeast ridge", pos: (75.0, 100.0), radius: 12.0),
    ],
)
